WEBVTT


00:00:22.541 --> 00:00:24.304
That was beautifuI.


00:00:25.143 --> 00:00:27.077
Yeah, my man Satie's no joke.


00:00:27.512 --> 00:00:30.970
This place is amazing.
Not exactly struggling.


00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:34.814
Yeah, I consider it a consolation prize
from parents who don't speak.


00:00:36.188 --> 00:00:38.281
Everybody should be here a little later.


00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:41.154
So I figure we should get right
before they start showing up, yeah?


00:00:41.259 --> 00:00:44.228
Look, those beats you gave me?


00:00:44.529 --> 00:00:46.793
They're good. I like them.


00:00:47.666 --> 00:00:50.931
- But they're abstract.
- What do you mean, abstract?


00:00:51.703 --> 00:00:53.398
They're not really danceable.


00:00:54.139 --> 00:00:55.231
Not danceable? What are you...


00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.638
You sound like them bubblehead cats
down at the club.


00:00:57.743 --> 00:00:59.677
I'm trying to push it.
That's why I wanted to work with you.


00:00:59.778 --> 00:01:03.111
You want people to like it,
and you want me to dance to it, right?


00:01:03.215 --> 00:01:06.048
- You can't dance to that?
- I can dance to anything.


00:01:06.618 --> 00:01:07.812
But not that?


00:01:09.554 --> 00:01:10.612
Wow.


00:01:11.757 --> 00:01:15.318
All right. All right. So, cooI. Tell me
what you want, and I'll work with you.


00:01:15.427 --> 00:01:17.952
- Hey, this was your idea.
- No, it's cooI.


00:01:18.997 --> 00:01:21.295
- You sure?
- Yeah, I'm sure.


00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:25.193
Okay. Track four.
Can you make it faster?


00:02:23.028 --> 00:02:25.223
Bloody long trek from that train.


00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:28.290
This is NigeI,
the director I was telling you about.


00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.494
It's a pleasure to meet you.
Miles tells me you're a genius.


00:02:31.603 --> 00:02:34.436
Are you sure
he wasn't talking about himself?


00:02:34.539 --> 00:02:36.370
All right, boys. Let's go.


00:02:39.077 --> 00:02:41.409
- What's up, man?
-50 bucks in Chinatown, baby.


00:02:41.513 --> 00:02:42.912
50 bucks.


00:02:43.748 --> 00:02:46.683
So NigeI thinks we have something hot.


00:02:47.252 --> 00:02:49.880
There's no way I could've done that
without you.


00:02:49.988 --> 00:02:52.422
- It was fun. You were right.
- I know.


00:02:52.524 --> 00:02:54.355
I wish I had more time
to do stuff like that.


00:02:54.459 --> 00:02:57.155
What?
You have all the time in the world.


00:02:57.496 --> 00:03:00.158
Not if I'm going to be
a prima ballerina by 21.


00:03:00.332 --> 00:03:02.596
That's really what you want to do, huh?


00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:04.168
That's the plan.


00:03:05.237 --> 00:03:07.228
Damn. All right.


00:03:07.405 --> 00:03:09.532
I was really hoping that,I don't know...


00:03:10.375 --> 00:03:11.967
me and you could,


00:03:13.612 --> 00:03:14.840
maybe...


00:03:15.981 --> 00:03:17.448
We could what?


00:03:22.287 --> 00:03:24.084
Get a cannoli or something?


00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:28.357
- A cannoli?
- Yeah, a cannoli.


00:03:38.737 --> 00:03:40.637
- I should get some rest.
- Yeah.


00:03:40.939 --> 00:03:43.499
<i>I got my Giselle audition in the morning.</i>


00:03:43.608 --> 00:03:44.905
Yeah, definitely.


00:03:45.644 --> 00:03:47.077
Good night.


00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.855
- What part are you auditioning for?
- Giselle.


00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.192
Whenever you're ready.


00:04:39.397 --> 00:04:41.627
Yo, NigeI showed me the edits.


00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.661
It is coconuts. You rocked it, girI.


00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:47.261
I can't wait to see it.


00:04:49.341 --> 00:04:51.775
- You look beat.
- I am beat.


00:04:51.876 --> 00:04:55.607
Well, give up them feet. It's time for
Dr. Miles' famous foot massage.


00:04:55.714 --> 00:04:58.148
- No, they're awfuI.
- Oh, no, no, no, no.


00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.411
My man Stef got feet
that look like monkey hands,


00:05:00.518 --> 00:05:02.986
so yours can't be that much worse.
Come on.


00:05:03.421 --> 00:05:05.787
- Come on.
- Okay.


00:05:06.124 --> 00:05:07.921
- Oh, my...
- I told you.


00:05:08.026 --> 00:05:09.584
Just playing.


00:05:14.699 --> 00:05:16.064
Feels good, right?


00:05:21.139 --> 00:05:23.039
So why you dancing ballet?


00:05:23.541 --> 00:05:24.838
What do you mean?


00:05:25.043 --> 00:05:29.980
I don't know. It's just so rigid.
You could do so much more.


00:05:31.983 --> 00:05:35.817
Oh, right.
I have the souI of a trombone player.


00:05:36.187 --> 00:05:37.211
Yes.


00:05:40.458 --> 00:05:43.450
I used to dream
about being this classicaI composer.


00:05:43.561 --> 00:05:46.257
I mean, pounding out notes
on the piano, hour after hour.


00:05:46.364 --> 00:05:48.161
I read every book
written on music theory.


00:05:48.266 --> 00:05:50.791
I wanted to write a symphony
by the time I turned 18.


00:05:50.902 --> 00:05:52.369
What happened?


00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:56.404
Wrote the sketches for my symphony.
Got it into Juilliard and got accepted.


00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.605
But you ended up quitting.


00:06:02.781 --> 00:06:03.839
Why?


00:06:08.486 --> 00:06:09.976
Dreams change.


00:06:14.292 --> 00:06:15.987
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!


00:06:16.094 --> 00:06:18.494
- I got the part in the play.
- The quirky brunette?


00:06:18.596 --> 00:06:21.997
- No, the dumb blonde.
- Oh, my God. That's great!


00:06:25.804 --> 00:06:28.671
God, gross.
You're touching her ballerina feet.


00:06:29.374 --> 00:06:31.137
Okay, you know what?
If you guys are going to do that,


00:06:31.242 --> 00:06:33.267
one, wear gloves.


00:06:33.545 --> 00:06:35.172
And two, just...


00:06:40.552 --> 00:06:43.112
<i>How do you know when you're
performing a movement perfectly?</i>


00:06:43.221 --> 00:06:46.247
You feeI perfect. You are the
movement.


00:06:46.925 --> 00:06:50.691
Everything is working within you
and through you.


00:06:52.564 --> 00:06:54.828
All effort falls away.


00:06:56.401 --> 00:06:58.369
You disappear into the dance.


00:06:59.604 --> 00:07:03.005
And all that's left
is the purity of the spirit


00:07:03.875 --> 00:07:05.035
and emotion.


00:07:09.013 --> 00:07:10.139
Bella.


00:07:10.982 --> 00:07:13.382
Sara, first line.


00:07:16.388 --> 00:07:18.720
Katrina, could you get the bars please?


00:07:19.958 --> 00:07:21.550
Well, I'd love Giselle.


00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.990
I'll be anything
as long as it isn't a peasant.


00:07:24.095 --> 00:07:25.392
I can't stand being a peasant.


00:07:25.497 --> 00:07:27.522
But I'd be happy
with the Queen of the Wilis.


00:07:27.632 --> 00:07:29.725
- Have you ever been a peasant?
- No.


00:07:29.834 --> 00:07:32.428
Well, it's all these
little folksy steps and this...


00:07:34.773 --> 00:07:37.333
I just can't bear it again.


00:07:37.609 --> 00:07:39.304
- Oh, my God.
- There it is.


00:07:44.315 --> 00:07:46.943
Katrina got Giselle.
Well, no surprise there.


00:07:47.385 --> 00:07:50.013
But you got Queen of the Wilis.


00:07:50.889 --> 00:07:53.380
Looks like I'm going to be doing this
for the next six weeks.


00:07:53.491 --> 00:07:55.550
- Okay, see you.
- Oh, where are you going?


00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.423
I gotta get to my opening.


00:08:07.272 --> 00:08:09.502
- In a minute. Just a minute.
- Come on.


00:08:09.941 --> 00:08:11.067
In a minute.


00:08:16.815 --> 00:08:19.613
- Look at you.
- What do you think?


00:08:20.452 --> 00:08:22.750
I like it. It's hip.


00:08:22.854 --> 00:08:26.290
- There's a little hop in there, too.
- They're about to start again.


00:08:26.391 --> 00:08:28.018
Come on. Let's go.


00:08:28.126 --> 00:08:29.593
Can't wait to see your new dance piece.


00:08:29.694 --> 00:08:31.719
I need to get some fresh air,
so you guys go ahead.


00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:32.854
- Okay.
- I'll see you inside.


00:08:32.964 --> 00:08:34.192
Be in there.


00:08:47.679 --> 00:08:51.115
You're one of Monique's girls.
Sara, isn't it?


00:08:51.216 --> 00:08:52.581
Yes, that's right.


00:08:52.684 --> 00:08:55.380
Simone Eldaire. I head
the Modern Department at Juilliard.


00:08:55.487 --> 00:08:58.012
I know who you are.
It's an honor to meet you.


00:08:58.122 --> 00:09:00.750
I saw your piece. You were quite good.


00:09:01.459 --> 00:09:04.587
- Who choreographed it?
- I did.


00:09:06.631 --> 00:09:07.962
Congratulations.


00:09:09.267 --> 00:09:10.393
Thank you.


00:09:10.568 --> 00:09:12.559
You've put quite a spell on Monique.


00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:15.332
Whenever I see her,
she just goes on about you.


00:09:15.607 --> 00:09:16.801
Really?


00:09:19.644 --> 00:09:21.134
Our secret.


00:09:21.679 --> 00:09:23.670
I'm down to just one a day.


00:09:23.781 --> 00:09:26.716
Oh, the things we dancers do
to our bodies.


00:09:28.286 --> 00:09:31.983
Ms. Eldaire, if it's okay,
can we just keep this between us?


00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.251
- I'm really not supposed to...
- DeaI.


00:09:40.265 --> 00:09:43.098
Stop by my office
if you ever want to just talk


00:09:43.201 --> 00:09:46.193
about dance, boys, whatever.


00:09:46.304 --> 00:09:49.137
I know Monique can be a bit severe.


00:09:50.108 --> 00:09:51.473
Thank you. I will.


00:09:52.744 --> 00:09:54.041
It was a pleasure meeting you, Sara.


00:09:54.145 --> 00:09:56.613
I look forward to seeing
more of your work.


00:10:03.021 --> 00:10:04.113
Yes.


00:10:09.761 --> 00:10:13.492
What? Oh, my God!


00:10:13.598 --> 00:10:15.190
Are you kidding me?


00:10:57.275 --> 00:11:00.176
<i>The Vibe is at our party.
Do you know what this means?</i>


00:11:00.278 --> 00:11:02.439
This means... This means exposure.


00:11:02.547 --> 00:11:04.515
This means I'm not gonna
have to spend 25 minutes


00:11:04.616 --> 00:11:08.484
explaining my music to people, they just
gonna hear it and they gonna feeI it.


00:11:08.586 --> 00:11:11.953
- I'm so happy for you.
- By me, you mean us, right?


00:11:12.256 --> 00:11:16.386
Miles, this was supposed to be
a one-time deaI. I've got schooI.


00:11:16.494 --> 00:11:18.189
Wow! Right.


00:11:18.396 --> 00:11:20.694
Hey, can't do it, can't do it, right?


00:11:22.734 --> 00:11:26.693
<i>Okay, I've got Giselle rehearsals
four times a week,</i>


00:11:26.804 --> 00:11:31.298
and if I drop Intro to Hip-Hop,
since I get private tutoring anyway,


00:11:31.809 --> 00:11:34.243
- I could do it.
- That would be dope.


00:11:51.462 --> 00:11:54.329
<i>The Vibe guys said
we could have all the time we need.</i>


00:11:56.901 --> 00:11:57.959
Wow.


00:11:58.603 --> 00:12:01.766
- What's all this?
- That is my entire life on tape.


00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.765
- How many are there?
- I lost count.


00:12:04.876 --> 00:12:06.741
Over 8,000 hours at least.


00:12:07.412 --> 00:12:08.401
How did you...


00:12:08.513 --> 00:12:10.947
I just always carry around
a tape recorder.


00:12:11.215 --> 00:12:13.809
Started when I was young.
I was just a kid.


00:12:14.485 --> 00:12:17.113
First sound I remember
was the sound of rings jingling


00:12:17.221 --> 00:12:20.247
on the shower-curtain rod
when my mom was giving me a bath.


00:12:20.358 --> 00:12:22.451
- You got a tape of that?
- No. I was four.


00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:24.188
Let me see.


00:12:24.696 --> 00:12:26.823
Let me see. Let me see. Let me see.


00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:30.660
Come on.


00:12:37.608 --> 00:12:38.905
Have a seat.


00:12:47.885 --> 00:12:50.979
- What are we...
- Just listen.


00:13:00.031 --> 00:13:01.362
What is that?


00:13:03.468 --> 00:13:08.201
New York City, East River.
February 27, 1989.


00:13:09.273 --> 00:13:13.573
After five weeks below freezing,
the ice finally breaking.


00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:14.395
Concentrate.


00:15:16.601 --> 00:15:18.034
- You're okay.
- Yeah, I'm all right.


00:15:18.135 --> 00:15:19.693
Watch your turnout.


00:15:21.472 --> 00:15:22.939
Straighten up the line.


00:15:27.745 --> 00:15:28.803
Oh.


00:15:29.013 --> 00:15:31.777
- Katrina.
- You okay?


00:15:31.883 --> 00:15:33.248
- Get away from me. I'm fine.
- You sure?


00:15:33.351 --> 00:15:34.511
- Fine.
- Let's get you up gently.


00:15:34.619 --> 00:15:35.608
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine.


00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.120
- Can you take her to the clinic, please?
- Sure.


00:15:38.222 --> 00:15:39.246
I'm fine.


00:15:41.092 --> 00:15:44.255
So, in line. Let's go on.


00:15:47.798 --> 00:15:50.323
Bella, and...


00:16:07.118 --> 00:16:09.450
- What?
- Wake up, man.


00:16:10.054 --> 00:16:12.579
<i>Seriously, you've been all
Barney & Friends</i>


00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:15.352
ever since what's-her-name
scrambled your brains.


00:16:15.459 --> 00:16:18.656
- Am not.
- You two are like Bonnie and Clyde,


00:16:19.063 --> 00:16:20.860
Pam and Tommy Lee,


00:16:21.499 --> 00:16:23.967
- Bert and Ernie.
- All right.


00:16:24.068 --> 00:16:26.036
- Lewis and Clark.
- What?


00:16:26.137 --> 00:16:29.300
- Britney and Justin.
- They broke up.


00:16:29.407 --> 00:16:31.773
Seriously, man, you are so hooked.


00:16:32.209 --> 00:16:35.372
<i>It's like watching Bassmasters
on late night cable.</i>


00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:38.876
"And for tackle today,
we're using an eight-pound test line


00:16:38.983 --> 00:16:41.144
"and a blonde ballerina as bait. "


00:16:43.087 --> 00:16:44.884
- Get out of here, man.
- You're hooked.


00:16:44.989 --> 00:16:46.456
All right, whatever.


00:16:50.828 --> 00:16:53.194
- You're hooked.
- All right, Eraserhead.


00:16:54.899 --> 00:16:58.232
<i>Hooked
Hooked on</i>


00:16:58.336 --> 00:16:59.394
Oh, that sells.


00:16:59.503 --> 00:17:01.368
The doctor said it was just a sprain.


00:17:01.472 --> 00:17:04.270
The doctor told me
you have permanent ligament damage.


00:17:04.375 --> 00:17:05.967
But Miss Delacroix...


00:17:06.444 --> 00:17:08.810
I'm sorry, Katrina. You can't dance.


00:17:18.622 --> 00:17:20.180
So who gets Giselle?


00:17:26.697 --> 00:17:28.164
It's Sara, isn't it?


00:17:34.605 --> 00:17:38.666
She's making a fooI of you.
Ask your son.


00:17:43.247 --> 00:17:45.442
Five, six, seven, eight.


00:17:53.457 --> 00:17:55.618
Yo, stop, stop. Hold up.


00:17:56.761 --> 00:18:00.253
We can't even hear the drums with all
these horns blaring all over the place!


00:18:00.364 --> 00:18:02.161
Okay. You know what?
I'm really sick and tired of all your...


00:18:02.266 --> 00:18:04.496
Hey, why don't we just take a break?


00:18:06.504 --> 00:18:09.405
I really don't know, man.
Who does she think she is?


00:18:13.911 --> 00:18:16.573
- What?
- You're amazing.


00:18:18.949 --> 00:18:20.246
So are you.


00:18:23.587 --> 00:18:26.021
There's something I need to talk to you
about, actually...


00:18:26.123 --> 00:18:28.683
Can we not take so many breaks
here today?


00:18:28.793 --> 00:18:30.385
Some of us have a life.


00:18:35.733 --> 00:18:36.859
What is it?


00:18:39.603 --> 00:18:40.763
It's nothing.


00:18:42.673 --> 00:18:45.005
All right, let's take it from the top.


00:18:45.109 --> 00:18:47.407
Five, six, seven, eight.


00:19:01.525 --> 00:19:04.289
- You really did a job this time.
- This has nothing to do with you.


00:19:04.395 --> 00:19:06.795
You're right.
It has everything to do with her.


00:19:06.897 --> 00:19:08.922
Jesus, you don't care about her!


00:19:09.033 --> 00:19:10.728
- You need her...
- She's gifted...


00:19:10.835 --> 00:19:13.065
- ... more than she needs you.
- ... the way you were.


00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.764
- But you threw yours away.
- Please.


00:19:15.873 --> 00:19:18.467
For what? So some kids
on the street could know your name.


00:19:18.576 --> 00:19:20.840
My dream changed. That's all.


00:19:20.945 --> 00:19:23.539
I think you're just ashamed of
where you come from.


00:19:23.647 --> 00:19:26.878
No. I'm ashamed that you can't accept
that my history is out there


00:19:26.984 --> 00:19:29.009
and not inside this
white marble mausoleum.


00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:31.088
- You sound like your father.
- Fancy that.


00:19:31.188 --> 00:19:33.349
You're angry at me, be angry at me.
But let her alone.


00:19:33.457 --> 00:19:34.549
I love her.


00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:43.658
Well, good.


00:19:45.102 --> 00:19:46.729
Let her live her dream.


00:19:47.571 --> 00:19:49.334
Don't destroy hers, as well.


00:20:03.821 --> 00:20:05.812
So just remember...


00:20:05.923 --> 00:20:07.288
- Sara.
- Yes?


00:20:07.391 --> 00:20:10.383
Could you do me a favor and get me
my notes from the last design meeting?


00:20:10.494 --> 00:20:11.791
They're on my desk.


00:20:11.896 --> 00:20:13.659
- Sure.
- Bye.


00:20:48.599 --> 00:20:50.396
Sara, I...


00:20:52.670 --> 00:20:57.607
I tried. I tried to tell you in the park,
in rehearsaI...


00:20:59.577 --> 00:21:02.740
I wanted to tell you.
I just didn't know how to step to you.


00:21:02.846 --> 00:21:04.404
I still don't.


00:21:04.882 --> 00:21:06.349
I was afraid I'd lose you.


00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:10.284
And I knew if it came down to me
or ballet, you'd choose ballet.


00:21:12.323 --> 00:21:14.291
- I love you...
- Don't say that.


00:21:17.528 --> 00:21:18.961
I believed you.


00:21:21.265 --> 00:21:24.996
I believed that someone who can
create music as beautifully as you


00:21:25.102 --> 00:21:27.400
had to be telling the truth.


00:21:35.579 --> 00:21:39.538
You know what, Miles?
You're just another player.


00:21:47.358 --> 00:21:51.886
Yes, I know Miles was a totaI jerk, but...


00:21:51.996 --> 00:21:56.365
You know, it's not like his mother
is a freaking saint, either.


00:21:57.201 --> 00:22:00.227
Okay.
This happens to me way too much.


00:22:00.337 --> 00:22:02.168
I'm a dumb blonde.


00:22:02.539 --> 00:22:03.870
I'm gonna go now.


00:22:08.512 --> 00:22:09.740
Sara.


00:22:10.648 --> 00:22:12.479
I want you to dance Giselle.


00:22:16.487 --> 00:22:18.045
Everything all right?


00:22:19.556 --> 00:22:22.252
- I feeI like such an idiot.
- Don't.


00:22:22.359 --> 00:22:25.954
Miles has never cared what effect
his actions have on other people.


00:22:26.063 --> 00:22:28.054
I've arranged for you to be moved
to a single room,


00:22:28.165 --> 00:22:29.894
so you can concentrate
on your preparation.


00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.026
- I don't need to.
- You need to rest. Get some sleep.


00:24:14.271 --> 00:24:17.331
Stop! PauI, just cut it out!


00:24:17.674 --> 00:24:19.403
You know you're not supposed
to stick out.


00:24:19.510 --> 00:24:21.603
You're supposed to blend.
You're a peasant.


00:24:21.712 --> 00:24:23.179
I'm coming up there.


00:24:24.381 --> 00:24:27.441
Sara. Hey, Miles doesn't know
I'm telling you this so...


00:24:27.551 --> 00:24:28.916
And he'd probably beat me up
if he found out,


00:24:29.019 --> 00:24:30.145
so, please don't tell him, okay?


00:24:30.254 --> 00:24:32.085
- Okay.
- He needs you.


00:24:32.189 --> 00:24:33.588
The dancers won't listen to him,


00:24:33.690 --> 00:24:35.157
everything's falling apart.
Luckily, the guys...


00:24:35.259 --> 00:24:38.160
<i>I can't do anything, okay. I have Giselle.</i>


00:24:39.296 --> 00:24:40.490
I'm sorry.


00:24:41.765 --> 00:24:43.255
Okay, fine. That's cooI.


00:24:43.367 --> 00:24:45.528
No. No, that's not cooI.


00:24:45.636 --> 00:24:47.069
Look, whatever happened
between you and Miles


00:24:47.171 --> 00:24:48.570
doesn't mean you can't help out.


00:24:48.672 --> 00:24:50.833
- You just don't want to.
- That's not fair.


00:24:50.941 --> 00:24:55.139
You're like mini-Monique. Jeté, jeté.


00:24:55.245 --> 00:24:58.806
- Zoe.
- I feeI like I swallowed a bug.


00:25:03.454 --> 00:25:05.445
Sara, we can't come to your ballet.


00:25:05.556 --> 00:25:06.818
It's not 'cause of Zoe or anything,


00:25:06.924 --> 00:25:09.757
it's just we have dress rehearsaI
that night and...


00:25:09.893 --> 00:25:12.361
Well, we need all the rehearsaI
we can get.


00:25:13.263 --> 00:25:14.491
Sorry.


00:25:15.566 --> 00:25:16.863
I understand.


00:25:25.175 --> 00:25:27.541
Sara, can you come up on stage,
please?


00:25:27.644 --> 00:25:28.702
Yes.


00:25:40.724 --> 00:25:42.351
Watch that rouge.


00:25:44.228 --> 00:25:45.422
Ta-da!


00:25:46.964 --> 00:25:49.558
- Isn't it lovely?
- What's it for?


00:25:52.035 --> 00:25:55.300
I'm having a dinner party
after the performance at my home.


00:25:56.306 --> 00:25:58.240
Absolutely everyone will be there,


00:25:58.342 --> 00:26:01.539
even the Chairman of the board
of American Ballet Theatre.


00:26:03.080 --> 00:26:04.377
Are you pleased?


00:26:10.487 --> 00:26:13.923
- Are you nervous?
- Yes.


00:26:14.024 --> 00:26:17.187
You shouldn't be. You're my student.


00:26:17.561 --> 00:26:21.930
Now remember to watch
those extensions and think up.


00:26:22.566 --> 00:26:23.533
<i>Merde.</i>


00:26:37.581 --> 00:26:38.548
Excuse me, you can't go...


00:26:38.649 --> 00:26:41.846
Yeah, yeah, yeah, I know her.
Thank you.


00:26:43.287 --> 00:26:45.847
- Wow, look at you.
- Hey, okay, no, no, no.


00:26:45.956 --> 00:26:48.982
Don't be nice yet, okay?


00:26:49.126 --> 00:26:51.594
There are two things. No.


00:26:56.300 --> 00:27:00.930
"I just wanted to say that I'm sorry


00:27:01.038 --> 00:27:02.369
"and that I love you so much.


00:27:02.472 --> 00:27:05.498
"Because no matter how stupid or crazy
I act, you've always been there for me.


00:27:05.609 --> 00:27:08.806
"And I'm sorry. Break a leg. Love, Zoe. "


00:27:10.414 --> 00:27:13.474
- It's okay.
- No, no, no, it's not okay,


00:27:13.584 --> 00:27:16.246
'cause I was such a bitch and...


00:27:16.353 --> 00:27:18.514
God, I am so proud of you, Sara.


00:27:18.722 --> 00:27:22.886
You did it. You know, you did
what you said you were going to do.


00:27:23.660 --> 00:27:26.925
- You're so rad.
- You're the rad one.


00:27:27.197 --> 00:27:30.132
- And so blonde.
- I know.


00:27:31.401 --> 00:27:34.029
I kind of like being a dumb blonde.


00:27:35.005 --> 00:27:37.235
You know I think Franz likes it, too.


00:27:37.341 --> 00:27:38.831
Men are so easy.


00:27:39.142 --> 00:27:42.168
<i>Fifteen minutes to places, please.
Fifteen minutes.</i>


00:27:42.779 --> 00:27:46.943
You have some twirling to do.
I'm gonna try and not whistle too loud.


00:27:47.050 --> 00:27:48.950
Wait. You said two things.


00:27:49.386 --> 00:27:50.876
Please don't hate me.


00:27:51.088 --> 00:27:54.080
I nearly killed Franz
when he asked me to do this.


00:27:56.193 --> 00:27:57.922
It's from Miles.


00:32:26.696 --> 00:32:28.493
WonderfuI!


00:32:30.667 --> 00:32:32.430
Giselle!


00:33:07.270 --> 00:33:09.204
Oh, great job.


00:33:09.306 --> 00:33:11.399
- It was great. It was wonderfuI.
- Good, good, good, thank you.


00:33:24.955 --> 00:33:27.321
Sara, there you are.


00:33:28.792 --> 00:33:31.056
What on earth are you doing here?


00:33:31.861 --> 00:33:34.193
Everyone wants to congratulate you.


00:33:39.502 --> 00:33:40.867
What's the matter?


00:33:41.938 --> 00:33:43.371
Is something wrong?


00:33:46.876 --> 00:33:49.003
Oh, you must be exhausted.


00:33:49.679 --> 00:33:52.842
I can remember coming off stage
after a performance,


00:33:52.949 --> 00:33:54.849
barely able to walk.


00:33:56.419 --> 00:33:58.478
You leave everything on the stage.


00:34:00.123 --> 00:34:02.250
It's the best feeling in the world.


00:34:07.030 --> 00:34:10.898
- Did you ever wonder if...
- What?


00:34:12.602 --> 00:34:16.197
- If it was enough?
- Enough?


00:34:19.075 --> 00:34:23.239
Dear girI, once you get a taste for it,
it's never enough.


00:34:23.580 --> 00:34:26.549
In time, there are better sets,
lovelier costumes...


00:34:26.649 --> 00:34:27.741
No.


00:34:28.985 --> 00:34:33.513
Did you ever wonder
if this was all you'd ever do,


00:34:33.623 --> 00:34:35.181
all you'd ever be?


00:34:35.425 --> 00:34:38.053
Let's go. Everyone's waiting.


00:34:38.428 --> 00:34:42.228
Miss Delacroix, I don't think
I want to be just a ballerina.


00:34:42.332 --> 00:34:44.698
- It's just nerves.
- You're not listening.


00:34:45.335 --> 00:34:47.803
I can't give up everything for ballet.


00:34:47.904 --> 00:34:49.531
No one's asking you
to give up everything.


00:34:49.639 --> 00:34:50.970
But you will.


00:34:51.374 --> 00:34:55.140
Maybe not on purpose,
maybe not all at once.


00:34:59.182 --> 00:35:03.084
Listen to me, Sara,
there are hundreds of thousands of girls


00:35:03.186 --> 00:35:05.381
who would kill to be in your position.


00:35:05.488 --> 00:35:10.221
Your gift means nothing
without hard work, discipline


00:35:10.960 --> 00:35:14.020
and yes, sacrifice.


00:35:14.831 --> 00:35:17.527
You just have a child's idea
of happiness.


00:35:18.802 --> 00:35:21.930
And to be great you have to...
You have to let that go.


00:35:24.274 --> 00:35:25.571
Why?


00:35:28.111 --> 00:35:30.011
I'll wait for you in the limo.


00:35:30.613 --> 00:35:33.047
I'm sorry. I can't go to your party.


00:35:52.469 --> 00:35:54.960
- You changed the song again!
- I had to.


00:35:55.071 --> 00:35:58.268
And I'm just supposed to redo
all the steps?


00:35:58.408 --> 00:36:00.239
This is your mess, you fix it.


00:36:00.343 --> 00:36:02.277
- Candy, please.
- No.


00:36:02.378 --> 00:36:05.609
You holler when you sort it all out,
Mr. ControI Freak!


00:36:05.715 --> 00:36:08.445
You know the number,
unless you changed that, too.


00:36:11.521 --> 00:36:14.820
Miles, what are we gonna do now?


00:36:15.758 --> 00:36:18.386
I don't know, man.
Just give me a minute.


00:36:31.741 --> 00:36:35.768
- Sara, I...
- No, don't say anything.


00:36:38.014 --> 00:36:39.447
Please just listen.


00:36:40.316 --> 00:36:43.149
I danced the best
I've ever danced tonight.


00:36:44.154 --> 00:36:46.019
It was close to perfect.


00:36:47.223 --> 00:36:50.488
When I was done, I closed my eyes


00:36:50.593 --> 00:36:53.027
and I felt such peace.


00:36:54.197 --> 00:36:55.892
But when I opened them,


00:36:57.200 --> 00:37:01.068
everyone was standing and clapping.


00:37:03.706 --> 00:37:06.072
And I felt nothing.


00:37:09.679 --> 00:37:10.976
Just numb.


00:37:12.715 --> 00:37:16.481
And I thought to myself,
"That's an odd thing to feeI.


00:37:16.819 --> 00:37:20.220
"I've worked my whole life
to get to this place,


00:37:20.790 --> 00:37:22.690
"and I feeI nothing?"


00:37:24.761 --> 00:37:27.252
And then there you were.


00:37:29.165 --> 00:37:31.258
You popped into my head.


00:37:32.068 --> 00:37:34.400
I couldn't stop thinking about you.


00:37:35.872 --> 00:37:40.366
Your face, your smile,
and what you said that day in class.


00:37:41.444 --> 00:37:43.173
"I am here. "


00:37:52.689 --> 00:37:57.388
And I realized this whole time, I've been
trying to perfect someone else's steps


00:37:57.527 --> 00:37:59.620
instead of finding my own.


00:38:01.364 --> 00:38:03.457
Well, I wanna be here, too.


00:38:04.867 --> 00:38:08.234
I wanna paint with ballerinas, b-boys


00:38:08.338 --> 00:38:10.533
in point shoes and high-tops.


00:38:11.874 --> 00:38:15.002
If my dream of dancing ballet


00:38:15.111 --> 00:38:17.375
doesn't have enough room for all that,


00:38:17.480 --> 00:38:20.745
my friends,
and you with a cannoli once in a while,


00:38:22.719 --> 00:38:25.984
then I'm gonna have to find a dream
big enough that does.


00:38:27.824 --> 00:38:30.691
And all I was gonna say was,
"I'm sorry. "


00:38:43.239 --> 00:38:46.367
So, looks like you're having
some trouble with your dancers.


00:38:46.476 --> 00:38:50.742
Yeah. We got 24 hours to get right,
and we looking kind of wrong right now.


00:38:50.847 --> 00:38:52.542
You know what I'm saying?


00:38:55.184 --> 00:38:56.617
You want some help?


00:39:00.790 --> 00:39:03.020
You're not gonna make me beg,
are you?


00:39:05.695 --> 00:39:09.290
Miles, please let me help you.


00:39:11.968 --> 00:39:13.128
All right.


00:42:56.092 --> 00:42:57.059
<i>I'm out.</i>

